From af534b63c8967a20ca782a27680242e79aebe356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:43:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 337/638] blink: move Platform constituents behind resident
 seam

In the AROS resident Platform consumer mode, retain each constituent target's generated-header, configuration, and dependency contract while suppressing its implementation sources. Core reaches callable Platform/WTF APIs through the already generated blink_platform.library bridge.

AI_PHASE: chromium-blink-core-library

AI_STATUS: platform-constituent-suppression-assumption-checkpoint

AI_ASSUMPTION: removing the 244 retained Platform constituent objects will expose the real Core-to-Platform data ABI boundary without breaking compile-time header generation

AI_VALIDATION: first focused Core archive passed 14951/14951 and classified constituents as scheduler=73, loader=66, wtf=46, network=19, image-decoders=16, instrumentation=13, heap=5, blob=5, avx=1

AI_EVIDENCE: out/aros-blink-core/test-artifacts/-blink-core-library-20260725/04-focused-core-archive-audit.log

AI_LIMITATIONS: focused GN regeneration and archive rebuild are pending; 646 known data-object crossings are not synthesized by the callable bridge

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:; 1d3cc6f4e1; V8 d1f9493
